// The three byte codes this lexer names. Each magic number gets exactly one
// accessor (NOTES.md section 6): two constant functions returning the same
// literal would be a duplicate-logic error, and one accessor per code makes
// that impossible by construction.

ch_dq() {
} return int 34;

ch_sq() {
} return int 39;

ch_nl() {
} return int 10;
